  "notes": "Re-extracted from the re-trimmed PDF (13 pages; p13 County Treasurer Activity schedule newly added). Governmental funds cash basis (Total Governmental Funds column p4; Eliminations column removes the 294 General-to-Street transfer, so Total prints transfers in 588,075 / out 46,232). Fund balance roll-forward 831,735 + 1,253,798 - 1,668,956 + 588,075 - 46,232 = 958,420. Beginning and ending cash null (no single governmental cash total printed; cash lines are in balance_sheet), as in FY2024. Aligned with FY2024: Property taxes 210,084 (p4) split using the County Treasurer Activity schedule (p13), whose total revenues collected equal it exactly (167,476 + 18,115 + 376 + 15,496 + 287 + 8,593 - 1,846 + 1,587); Sales and other taxes 122,972 split using budget schedule lines (p8): sales tax 94,224 + motor vehicle tax 20,903 + other state receipts 7,845; Fees, taxes, permits and licenses split by fund column. Business-type 'Other' revenue kept other: the FY2023 Statement of Activities (p2) counts it in Miscellaneous (business-type Charges for Services 1,871,394 = Sales only). Business-type accrual (net position): 2,800,808 + 1,888,602 - 1,239,711 - 541,843 = 2,907,856. Proprietary cash flows null as in FY2024 (cash-basis report). Detail: County Treasurer schedule (p13) and the four utility schedules (pp9-12, which sum to the proprietary statement); no governmental statement-column lines (as FY2024); the all-funds budget comparison (p8) is combined governmental+utility and not recorded. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
